  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Exploded Stack\n\nIsometric layer plates sit as one stack, explode apart along the vertical axis with labels drawing in beside each layer, hold, then collapse back so the clip loops. Four layers with their own glyph motifs and an accent colour.\n\nCategory: motion-graphics. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- An architecture or stack explainer: four labelled layers that separate, are called out one by one and collapse again.\n- A loopable isometric diagram for a product or system overview.\n\nAvoid when:\n- More than four layers: the block is built for four.\n- A flat 2D diagram.\n\nVariables:\n- title (string): Title, default \"How a request moves\"\n- layer_1 (string): Top layer, default \"Interface\"\n- layer_2 (string): Layer 2, default \"API gateway\"\n- layer_3 (string): Layer 3, default \"Services\"\n- layer_4 (string): Bottom layer, default \"Data\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#0a84ff\"\n- background (color): Backdrop, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Exploded Stack\n\n  Isometric layer plates sit as one stack, explode apart along the vertical axis with labels drawing in beside each layer, hold, then collapse back so the clip loops. Four layers with their own glyph motifs and an accent colour.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes/blob/bd6cff8157a1a0ed5075527e673cc4f321fe9123/registry/blocks/exploded-stack/exploded-stack.html\n\n  Copyright HeyGen, Inc. and the Hyperframes contributors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version\n  2.0 (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain\n  a copy of the License at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable\n  law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n  BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for\n  the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: fills the host frame (on a vertical frame the isometric view is widened and the title, labels and leader lines scale from the shorter side); rewritten from three.js (not loaded) to raw WebGL2 with an orthographic isometric camera: plates are square-cornered boxes with the same stacking, explode and collapse timing, the contact shadow and glyph motifs are drawn the same way, lighting is approximated with a hemisphere and one sun term; the font is Inter from Google Fonts; the canvas is drawn at the `resolution` variable.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"exploded-stack\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title\", \"default\": \"How a request moves\"},\n    {\"id\": \"layer_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Top layer\", \"default\": \"Interface\"},\n    {\"id\": \"layer_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Layer 2\", \"default\": \"API gateway\"},\n    {\"id\": \"layer_3\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Layer 3\", \"default\": \"Services\"},\n    {\"id\": \"layer_4\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Bottom layer\", \"default\": \"Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"default\": \"#0a84ff\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Backdrop\", \"default\": \"#f4f4f5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the plates are drawn at, then scaled up. Edges and hairlines need 0.75.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Exploded Stack</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@500;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .ges-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .ges-canvas {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .ges-title {\n          position: absolute;\n          left: 11cqmin;\n          top: 10cqmin;\n          font: 700 5.6cqmin / 1.1 \"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif;\n          letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n          color: #14161c;\n        }\n        .ges-leaders {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n        }\n        .ges-leaders line { stroke: rgba(27, 30, 39, 0.35); stroke-width: 2; }\n        .ges-label {\n          position: absolute;\n          left: 0;\n          top: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          align-items: center;\n          gap: 1.7cqmin;\n          font: 500 3.15cqmin / 1 \"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif;\n          color: #1b1e27;\n          white-space: nowrap;\n          opacity: 0;\n        }\n        .ges-index { font-size: 1.85cqmin; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"exploded-stack\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ges-clip\" class=\"ges-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"ges-canvas\" class=\"ges-canvas\"></canvas>\n          <svg id=\"ges-leaders\" class=\"ges-leaders\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n          <div id=\"ges-title\" class=\"ges-title\"></div>\n          <div id=\"ges-labels\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"exploded-stack\";\n            var DUR = 5;\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"ges-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#000000\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title\", \"default\": \"How a request moves\"}, {\"id\": \"layer_1\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Top layer\", \"default\": \"Interface\"}, {\"id\": \"layer_2\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Layer 2\", \"default\": \"API gateway\"}, {\"id\": \"layer_3\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Layer 3\", \"default\": \"Services\"}, {\"id\": \"layer_4\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Bottom layer\", \"default\": \"Data\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"default\": \"#0a84ff\"}, {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Backdrop\", \"default\": \"#f4f4f5\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the plates are drawn at, then scaled up. Edges and hairlines need 0.75.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * V.resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * V.resolution));\n            root.style.background = V.background;\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            document.getElementById(\"ges-title\").textContent = V.title;\n            var names = [V.layer_1, V.layer_2, V.layer_3, V.layer_4];\n            var U = Math.min(W, H) / 1080;\n            var labelsBox = document.getElementById(\"ges-labels\");\n            var leaders = document.getElementById(\"ges-leaders\");\n            leaders.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H);\n            var svgNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            var labelEls = [], indexEls = [], lines = [], dots = [];\n            names.forEach(function (name, i) {\n              var el = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              el.className = \"ges-label\";\n              el.innerHTML = '<span class=\"ges-index\">0' + (i + 1) + \"</span><span></span>\";\n              el.lastChild.textContent = name;\n              labelsBox.appendChild(el);\n              labelEls.push(el); indexEls.push(el.firstChild);\n              var line = document.createElementNS(svgNS, \"line\");\n              var dot = document.createElementNS(svgNS, \"circle\");\n              dot.setAttribute(\"r\", String(6 * U));\n              leaders.appendChild(line); leaders.appendChild(dot);\n              lines.push(line); dots.push(dot);\n            });\n            var ACCENT = rgb(V.accent);\n            // Isometric orthographic camera: 45 degrees round Y, looking down at arctan(1/sqrt 2); slid along\n            // its right axis so the stack sits left and the labels get the right.\n            var ASPECT = cw / ch;\n            var HALF_W = ASPECT >= 16 / 9 ? 5.9 * ASPECT : (ASPECT >= 1 ? 5.9 * 16 / 9 : 6.6);\n            var HALF_H = ASPECT >= 16 / 9 ? 5.9 : HALF_W / ASPECT;\n            var EYE = [10 + 1.9, 10.7, 10 - 1.9];\n            var FWD = [-1 / Math.sqrt(3), -1 / Math.sqrt(3), -1 / Math.sqrt(3)];\n            function cross(a, b) { return [a[1] * b[2] - a[2] * b[1], a[2] * b[0] - a[0] * b[2], a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0]]; }\n            function norm(v) { var l = Math.hypot(v[0], v[1], v[2]); return [v[0] / l, v[1] / l, v[2] / l]; }\n            var RIGHT = norm(cross(FWD, [0, 1, 0])), UP = cross(RIGHT, FWD);\n            function dot3(a, b) { return a[0] * b[0] + a[1] * b[1] + a[2] * b[2]; }\n            var N0 = 0.1, F0 = 100;\n            // view-projection (orthographic), column-major\n            var VP = new Float32Array([\n              RIGHT[0] / HALF_W, UP[0] / HALF_H, -FWD[0] * 2 / (F0 - N0) * -1 * -1, 0,\n              RIGHT[1] / HALF_W, UP[1] / HALF_H, 0, 0,\n              RIGHT[2] / HALF_W, UP[2] / HALF_H, 0, 0,\n              -dot3(RIGHT, EYE) / HALF_W, -dot3(UP, EYE) / HALF_H, 0, 1\n            ]);\n            // depth: z_clip = (2 * (dot(FWD, p - EYE) - N0) / (F0 - N0)) - 1, so nearer is smaller\n            var DK = 2 / (F0 - N0);\n            VP[2] = FWD[0] * DK; VP[6] = FWD[1] * DK; VP[10] = FWD[2] * DK; VP[14] = -dot3(FWD, EYE) * DK - (2 * N0 / (F0 - N0)) - 1;\n            function toScreen(p) {\n              var x = (dot3(RIGHT, p) - dot3(RIGHT, EYE)) / HALF_W, y = (dot3(UP, p) - dot3(UP, EYE)) / HALF_H;\n              return [(x * 0.5 + 0.5) * W, (-y * 0.5 + 0.5) * H];\n            }\n            // Plate textures: a white face with a hairline, and a glyph motif per layer (white on transparent).\n            function tex2d(draw) { var c = document.createElement(\"canvas\"); c.width = c.height = 512; draw(c.getContext(\"2d\")); return c; }\n            var faceCanvas = tex2d(function (g) { g.fillStyle = \"#ffffff\"; g.fillRect(0, 0, 512, 512); g.strokeStyle = \"#d6d8dd\"; g.lineWidth = 3; g.strokeRect(1.5, 1.5, 509, 509); });\n            var glyphCanvases = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(function (i) {\n              return tex2d(function (g) {\n                g.strokeStyle = g.fillStyle = \"#ffffff\"; g.lineWidth = 6;\n                var k, x, y;\n                if (i === 0) { for (k = 0; k < 3; k++) g.strokeRect(70 + k * 130, 150, 110, 212); }\n                else if (i === 1) { for (k = 0; k < 5; k++) { g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(80, 110 + k * 72); g.lineTo(432, 110 + k * 72); g.stroke(); } }\n                else if (i === 2) { for (y = 0; y < 3; y++) for (x = 0; x < 3; x++) g.fillRect(96 + x * 120, 96 + y * 120, 80, 80); }\n                else { for (k = 0; k < 3; k++) { g.beginPath(); g.ellipse(256, 150 + k * 100, 150, 40, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); g.stroke(); } }\n              });\n            });\n            var LAYERS = 4, THICK = 0.22, GAP = 1.55, BASE = 5;\n            var OPEN_AT = 0.3, OPEN_FOR = 0.9, OPEN_STAGGER = 0.06, LAND_AT = 1.25, LAND_EVERY = 0.7, DRAW = 0.3, FULL = 0.4, SETTLE = 0.3;\n            var CLOSE_AT = LAND_AT + (LAYERS - 1) * LAND_EVERY + 0.7, CLOSE_FOR = 0.6, CLOSE_STAGGER = 0.05, LIFT = 0.08;\n            function clamp01(x) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, x)); }\n            function ease(x) { var v = clamp01(x); return v < 0.5 ? 4 * v * v * v : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * v + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            function easeOut(x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - clamp01(x), 3); }\n            function easeOpen(x) { return easeOut(Math.pow(clamp01(x), 1.4)); }\n            function focus(T, i) { var land = LAND_AT + i * LAND_EVERY; return easeOut((T - land + DRAW) / DRAW) * (1 - ease((T - land - FULL) / SETTLE)); }\n            var GLYPH_REST = [0xc9 / 255, 0xcc / 255, 0xd3 / 255], INK_REST = [0x8b / 255, 0x90 / 255, 0x9a / 255];\n            function lerp3(a, b, t) { return [a[0] + (b[0] - a[0]) * t, a[1] + (b[1] - a[1]) * t, a[2] + (b[2] - a[2]) * t]; }\n            function css(c) { return \"rgb(\" + c.map(function (v) { return Math.round(v * 255); }).join(\",\") + \")\"; }\n\n            var VERTEX = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\nin vec3 aPos;\nin vec3 aNormal;\nin vec2 aUv;\nin float aKind;\nuniform mat4 uVP;\nuniform float uY;\nout vec2 vUv;\nout vec3 vN;\nout float vKind;\nvoid main() {\n  vUv = aUv;\n  vN = aNormal;\n  vKind = aKind;\n  gl_Position = uVP * vec4(aPos + vec3(0.0, uY, 0.0), 1.0);\n}`;\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\nout vec4 outColor;\nin vec2 vUv;\nin vec3 vN;\nin float vKind;\nuniform sampler2D uFace;\nuniform sampler2D uGlyph;\nuniform vec3 uGlyphCol;\nvoid main() {\n  if (vKind > 1.5) {\n    // soft contact shadow under the stack: premultiplied\n    float d = length(vUv - 0.5) * 2.0;\n    float a = 0.22 * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.3125, 1.0, d));\n    outColor = vec4(vec3(20.0, 24.0, 40.0) / 255.0 * a, a);\n    return;\n  }\n  vec3 n = normalize(vN);\n  float sky = n.y * 0.5 + 0.5;\n  vec3 hemi = mix(vec3(0.839, 0.851, 0.894), vec3(1.0), sky);\n  float sun = max(dot(n, normalize(vec3(-4.0, 10.0, 6.0))), 0.0);\n  float light = 0.78 + 0.0;\n  vec3 base = vec3(1.0);\n  if (vKind < 0.5) {\n    base = texture(uFace, vUv).rgb;\n    vec4 g = texture(uGlyph, vUv);\n    base = mix(base, uGlyphCol, g.a);\n  }\n  outColor = vec4(base * (hemi * light + sun * 0.3), 1.0);\n}\n`;\n\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { alpha: true, antialias: true, depth: true, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var prog = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(prog, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(prog);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(prog, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(prog) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(prog);\n              function boxVerts() {\n                var x = 2.1, y = THICK / 2, z = 2.1, v = [], faces = [\n                  [[-x, y, z], [x, y, z], [x, y, -z], [-x, y, -z], [0, 1, 0], 0],\n                  [[-x, -y, -z], [x, -y, -z], [x, -y, z], [-x, -y, z], [0, -1, 0], 1],\n                  [[-x, -y, z], [x, -y, z], [x, y, z], [-x, y, z], [0, 0, 1], 1],\n                  [[x, -y, -z], [-x, -y, -z], [-x, y, -z], [x, y, -z], [0, 0, -1], 1],\n                  [[x, -y, z], [x, -y, -z], [x, y, -z], [x, y, z], [1, 0, 0], 1],\n                  [[-x, -y, -z], [-x, -y, z], [-x, y, z], [-x, y, -z], [-1, 0, 0], 1]\n                ];\n                var uvs = [[0, 1], [1, 1], [1, 0], [0, 0]], idx = [0, 1, 2, 0, 2, 3];\n                faces.forEach(function (f) { idx.forEach(function (i) { v.push(f[i][0], f[i][1], f[i][2], f[4][0], f[4][1], f[4][2], uvs[i][0], uvs[i][1], f[5]); }); });\n                // the contact shadow: a 7 x 7 plane under the stack\n                var s = 3.5, sy = -2.4;\n                [[-s, sy, s, 0, 0], [s, sy, s, 1, 0], [s, sy, -s, 1, 1], [-s, sy, s, 0, 0], [s, sy, -s, 1, 1], [-s, sy, -s, 0, 1]].forEach(function (p) { v.push(p[0], p[1], p[2], 0, 1, 0, p[3], p[4], 2); });\n                return new Float32Array(v);\n              }\n              var buf = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buf);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, boxVerts(), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              [[\"aPos\", 3, 0], [\"aNormal\", 3, 12], [\"aUv\", 2, 24], [\"aKind\", 1, 32]].forEach(function (s) {\n                var loc = gl.getAttribLocation(prog, s[0]);\n                gl.enableVertexAttribArray(loc);\n                gl.vertexAttribPointer(loc, s[1], gl.FLOAT, false, 36, s[2]);\n              });\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              gl.enable(gl.DEPTH_TEST);\n              gl.enable(gl.BLEND);\n              gl.blendFunc(gl.ONE, gl.ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(prog, name); }\n              function makeTex(unit, source) {\n                var t = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, t);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, source);\n                return t;\n              }\n              makeTex(0, faceCanvas);\n              var glyphTex = glyphCanvases.map(function (c) { return makeTex(1, c); });\n              gl.uniform1i(u(\"uFace\"), 0);\n              gl.uniform1i(u(\"uGlyph\"), 1);\n              gl.uniformMatrix4fv(u(\"uVP\"), false, VP);\n              var yLoc = u(\"uY\"), glyphColLoc = u(\"uGlyphCol\");\n              paint = function (t) {\n\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT | gl.DEPTH_BUFFER_BIT);\n                var T = (t / DUR) * BASE, i;\n                // shadow first, then the plates (bottom to top)\n                gl.uniform1f(yLoc, 0);\n                gl.depthMask(false);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLES, 36, 6);\n                gl.depthMask(true);\n                for (i = 0; i < LAYERS; i++) {\n                  var order = LAYERS - 1 - i;\n                  var open = easeOpen((T - OPEN_AT - i * OPEN_STAGGER) / OPEN_FOR) - ease((T - CLOSE_AT - 0.05 - order * CLOSE_STAGGER) / CLOSE_FOR);\n                  var w = focus(T, i);\n                  var y = order * (THICK + 0.02 + open * GAP) - 2.2 + LIFT * w;\n                  var gc = lerp3(GLYPH_REST, ACCENT, w);\n                  gl.uniform1f(yLoc, y);\n                  gl.uniform3f(glyphColLoc, gc[0], gc[1], gc[2]);\n                  gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE1);\n                  gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, glyphTex[i]);\n                  gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLES, 0, 36);\n                  var ink = css(lerp3(INK_REST, ACCENT, w));\n                  indexEls[i].style.color = ink;\n                  dots[i].style.fill = ink;\n                  var shown = easeOut((T - LAND_AT - i * LAND_EVERY + DRAW) / DRAW) * (1 - clamp01((T - CLOSE_AT) / 0.2));\n                  // the plate's right-hand corner, where a label has open space beside it\n                  var a = toScreen([2.1, y, -2.1]);\n                  labelEls[i].style.opacity = shown.toFixed(3);\n                  labelEls[i].style.transform = \"translate(\" + Math.round(a[0] + 90 * U + 24 * U + (1 - shown) * 16 * U) + \"px, \" + Math.round(a[1] - 1.5 * 15 * U) + \"px)\";\n                  lines[i].setAttribute(\"x1\", a[0].toFixed(1)); lines[i].setAttribute(\"y1\", a[1].toFixed(1));\n                  lines[i].setAttribute(\"x2\", (a[0] + 90 * U * shown).toFixed(1)); lines[i].setAttribute(\"y2\", a[1].toFixed(1));\n                  lines[i].style.opacity = shown > 0 ? 1 : 0;\n                  dots[i].setAttribute(\"cx\", a[0].toFixed(1)); dots[i].setAttribute(\"cy\", a[1].toFixed(1));\n                  dots[i].style.opacity = shown.toFixed(3);\n                }\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              canvas.style.display = \"none\";\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true, onUpdate: function () { if (paint) paint(tl.time()); } });\n\n            // The block lasts DUR seconds even when nothing is tweened at the end.\n            tl.set({}, {}, DUR);\n            if (paint) paint(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
